WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.064
Watch and read: While at the market, Ama thinks about this: When reading your own

00:00:05.064 --> 00:00:06.685
writing aloud, what helps listeners?

00:00:07.533 --> 00:00:12.631
The answer is: A steady pace with clear words. Clarity and pace help listeners

00:00:12.631 --> 00:00:12.995
understand.

00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:19.182
Watch and read: Kojo is learning with a partner at school. Why should you notice

00:00:19.182 --> 00:00:20.245
punctuation while presenting?

00:00:21.117 --> 00:00:26.151
The answer is: It guides pauses and expression. Punctuation guides oral reading.
